            <!-- 1. The 6-Stage HADO Workflow -->
            <section class="content-section" id="hado-process">
                <h2>1. The 6-Stage Hardware Asset Disposal Order (HADO)</h2>
                <p>
                    Retiring enterprise hardware is fraught with regulatory and security risks: hard drives holding customer data can be leaked, environmental regulations (WEEE / EPA) can trigger massive fines, and unrecorded disposals lead to phantom assets on balance sheets.
                </p>
                <p>
                    In HAM Pro, physical disposal is managed through the <strong>Hardware Asset Disposal Order (<code>sn_hamp_disposal_order</code>)</strong>. Each stage of the order automatically spawns a mandatory child task (<code>sn_hamp_disposal_order_task</code>) that must be completed to advance the workflow.
                </p>

                <div class="diagram-block" style="margin: 28px 0;">
                    <div class="diagram-title">The 6-Stage Hardware Asset Disposal Order Lifecycle</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    stateDiagram-v2
                        direction LR
                        
                        Verify: Stage 1 Verify Assets
                        Schedule: Stage 2 Schedule Pickup
                        Transit: Stage 3 Asset Departure
                        Confirm: Stage 4 Vendor Confirmation
                        Document: Stage 5 Documentation / Resale
                        Complete: Stage 6 Closed Complete
                        
                        [*] --> Verify: Create HADO
                        Verify --> Schedule: Task 1 Closed
                        Schedule --> Transit: Task 2 Closed
                        Transit --> Confirm: Task 3 Closed
                        Confirm --> Document: Task 4 Closed
                        Document --> Complete: Task 5 Closed (CoD Attached)
                        Complete --> [*]
                        
                        note right of Verify
                            Task: Verify Assets
                            Add/remove serials, verify counts
                        end note
                        
                        note right of Transit
                            Task: Asset Departure
                            Cancellation LOCKED OUT after departure
                            Asset State: In Transit / Pending Disposal
                        end note
                        
                        note right of Document
                            Task: Disposal Documentation
                            Attach Certificate of Destruction (CoD)
                            Asset State: Retired / Disposed
                        end note
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="data-table-wrapper">
                    <table class="data-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Stage Number &amp; Name</th>
                                <th>Associated Task (Task Table)</th>
                                <th>Asset State / Substate Updates</th>
                                <th>Mandatory Operational Actions</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>1. Verify Assets</strong></td>
                                <td><code>Verify Assets</code></td>
                                <td><code>In Stock / Pending Disposal</code></td>
                                <td>Asset managers verify serial numbers and count pallets. Assets can still be added or removed from the order.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>2. Scheduling</strong></td>
                                <td><code>Schedule Pickup</code></td>
                                <td><code>In Stock / Pending Disposal</code></td>
                                <td>Coordinates with certified ITAD (IT Asset Disposition) vendor. Logs vendor name, contact, and scheduled loading dock pickup date.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>3. Transit</strong></td>
                                <td><code>Asset Departure</code></td>
                                <td><code>In Transit / Pending Disposal</code></td>
                                <td>Loading dock technicians scan assets onto vendor truck. <strong>Critical Rule:</strong> Disposal order cancellation is strictly locked out once this task is closed.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>4. Confirmation</strong></td>
                                <td><code>Vendor Confirmation</code></td>
                                <td><code>In Transit / Pending Disposal</code></td>
                                <td>ITAD vendor formally acknowledges physical arrival and receipt of shipment at processing plant.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>5. Documentation</strong></td>
                                <td><code>Disposal Documentation</code></td>
                                <td><code>Retired / Disposed</code></td>
                                <td>Technician attaches certified <strong>Certificate of Destruction (CoD)</strong> or resale credit slip. Sets final disposal date on records.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>6. Completed</strong></td>
                                <td><em>None (Order Closed)</em></td>
                                <td><code>Retired / Disposed</code></td>
                                <td>All financial balance sheet write-offs finalize. Active asset licenses revoked in SAM Pro.</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <div class="formula-block" style="margin-top: 28px;">
                    <div class="formula-content">
                        <em>Net Book Value Write-Off</em> <span class="formula-operator">=</span> <em>Original Acquisition Cost</em> <span class="formula-operator">&minus;</span> <em>Accumulated Depreciation</em> <span class="formula-operator">&minus;</span> <em>Vendor Resale Proceeds</em>
                    </div>
                    <div class="formula-caption">Financial Balance Sheet Asset Disposal Accounting Equation</div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 2. NIST Sanitization & CoD -->
            <section class="content-section" id="sanitization-cod">
                <h2>2. NIST 800-88 Data Sanitization &amp; Certificate of Destruction</h2>
                <p>
                    Data breaches occurring from improperly sanitized retired storage drives carry severe regulatory penalties (GDPR, HIPAA, PCI-DSS). HAM Pro enforces compliance with the <strong>NIST Special Publication 800-88 Revision 1 (Guidelines for Media Sanitization)</strong> framework.
                </p>

                <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top: 20px;">
                    <div class="card-basic">
                        <div style="color: var(--accent-primary); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;">NIST Tier 1</div>
                        <h4>Clear (Logical Overwrite)</h4>
                        <p>
                            Applies programmatic overwriting techniques using data sanitization software (e.g. Blancco). Rewrites all user-accessible storage locations with pseudorandom patterns. Suitable for hardware being redeployed internally.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card-basic">
                        <div style="color: var(--accent-secondary); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;">NIST Tier 2</div>
                        <h4>Purge (Cryptographic Erase)</h4>
                        <p>
                            Executes firmware-level Cryptographic Erase (CE) or degaussing for magnetic media. Renders target data completely unrecoverable even using state-of-the-art laboratory recovery techniques. Required for off-lease returns.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card-basic">
                        <div style="color: var(--accent-tertiary); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;">NIST Tier 3</div>
                        <h4>Destroy (Physical Shredding)</h4>
                        <p>
                            Physical destruction of media platters and solid-state NAND chips via industrial shredding (to 2mm particles), disintegration, or incineration. Required for top-secret and mission-critical enterprise systems.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="info-card info-card--important" style="margin-top: 24px;">
                    <div class="info-card-title">Certificate of Destruction (CoD) Audit Governance</div>
                    <p>
                        A disposal order cannot legally progress to <code>Completed</code> without a valid Certificate of Destruction attached to the documentation task. Every valid CoD must contain:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="feature-bullet-list">
                        <li>Exact chassis and hard drive serial numbers matching <code>alm_hardware.serial_number</code>.</li>
                        <li>Certified destruction method (NIST 800-88 Purge vs. Shred).</li>
                        <li>Date, time, and GPS facility coordinates of destruction event.</li>
                        <li>Witness signature and ITAD vendor EPA environmental facility license number.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 3. Hardware Refresh Orders -->
            <section class="content-section" id="refresh-orders">
                <h2>3. Hardware Asset Refresh Orders (<code>sn_hamp_refresh_order</code>)</h2>
                <p>
                    Maintaining obsolete hardware leads to ballooning maintenance costs and degraded worker productivity. HAM Pro automates scheduled PC and server hardware refresh cycles through <strong>Hardware Asset Refresh Orders</strong>.
                </p>

                <div class="diagram-block" style="margin: 28px 0;">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Automated Hardware Asset Refresh Lifecycle</div>
                    <div class="mermaid">
                    graph TD
                        Schedule["Scheduled Job:<br/>SAM - Calculate Asset Refresh Eligibility"] --> Eval{"Useful Life or Warranty<br/>Expired?"}
                        Eval -->|Yes| Flag["Set alm_hardware.eligible_for_refresh = true"]
                        
                        Flag --> Catalog["Submit Hardware Asset Refresh Order<br/>(sn_hamp_refresh_order)"]
                        Catalog --> LineFlow["Hardware Asset Refresh Line Flow<br/>(Flow Designer)"]
                        
                        LineFlow --> Task1["1. Prepare Task:<br/>Pick and Image Replacement Laptop"]
                        Task1 --> Task2["2. Schedule Task:<br/>Book Delivery Window with Employee"]
                        Task2 --> Task3["3. Deploy Task:<br/>Deliver Device and Migrate User Profile"]
                        Task3 --> Task4["4. Reclaim Task:<br/>Retrieve Aged Hardware and Route to HADO"]
                        
                        classDef default fill:#161b26,stroke:#334155,stroke-width:1px,color:#f8fafc
                        classDef highlight fill:#161b26,stroke:#10b981,stroke-width:2px,color:#f8fafc
                        classDef blue fill:#161b26,stroke:#3b82f6,stroke-width:2px,color:#f8fafc
                        class Flag,Catalog highlight
                        class LineFlow,Task1,Task2,Task3,Task4 blue
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="grid-2">
                    <div class="card-basic">
                        <h4>Eligibility Engine</h4>
                        <p>
                            A nightly scheduled job evaluates the <code>useful_life</code> (in months) on the Hardware Product Model against the asset's original purchase date:
                        </p>
                        <ul class="feature-bullet-list">
                            <li>Laptops: Typically configured for 36-month or 48-month refresh cycles.</li>
                            <li>Production Servers: Typically configured for 60-month refresh cycles.</li>
                            <li>Assets exceeding useful life are automatically stamped as eligible for refresh.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="card-basic">
                        <h4>Zero-Disruption Migration</h4>
                        <p>
                            The Refresh Line flow ensures employees are never without equipment:
                        </p>
                        <ul class="feature-bullet-list">
                            <li>The replacement device is fully imaged and shipped before the old device is touched.</li>
                            <li>The user receives a 5-day grace period to verify file transfers via OneDrive / cloud backup.</li>
                            <li>The old device is reclaimed, sanitized, and moved into the disposal queue.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

